# Line endings, made deterministic for every clone regardless of the
# cloner's core.autocrlf. The repository stores LF; the working copy gets
# what each consumer needs:
#   - VBA's VBComponents.Import requires CRLF to recognize a .cls file's
#     VERSION/BEGIN/END header (with LF the header lands in the code pane
#     as literal statements - a live, thrice-repeated incident). .bas/.frm
#     get the same treatment so the whole src/ tree imports uniformly.
#   - .vla phrasebooks and the prelude are read by VBA's own line reader,
#     which treats a bare LF as text, not a line break.
# Everything else is ordinary text (LF in the repo, platform default on
# checkout) or binary.
* text=auto
# The Cargo workspace (core/, cli/): Rust and its manifests are LF on every
# platform, as rustfmt writes them; a built .wasm is bytes.
*.rs text eol=lf
Cargo.toml text eol=lf
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
rust-toolchain.toml text eol=lf
*.wasm binary
*.bas text eol=crlf
*.cls text eol=crlf
*.frm text eol=crlf
*.vla text eol=crlf
*.frx binary
*.xlsm binary
*.xlam binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.ods binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
